==Icelandic==

===Alternative forms===
* [[jeg]] {{qualifier|before ''je'' → ''é'' reform}}
* [[eg]] {{qualifier|archaic, poetic}}
* [[ek]] {{qualifier|very archaic}}

===Etymology===
The Icelandic pronoun continues {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|ek}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*ek}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*éǵh₂}}. The pronoun is attested, in {{etyl|gmq-pro|is}} inscriptions, since at least the 3rd century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/jɛɣ/|[jɛːɣ]|lang=is}}
* {{audio|Is-ég.oga|Audio|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ɛːɣ|lang=is}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun|cat2=personal pronouns}}

